## [v7] AlphaProof Search Layer

### Core Insight
AlphaProof treats mathematical proof as tree search with AND/OR nodes. Cognitive task decomposition follows the same structure -- some tasks require ALL subtasks (AND), others require ANY path (OR).

### AND/OR Task Decomposition

**OR nodes** (standard): Multiple approaches, any one works.
```
"Fix this rendering bug"
|- [OR] Check shader compilation
|- [OR] Check texture bindings
\- [OR] Check viewport settings
-> Finding ONE solution proves the node
```

**AND nodes** (product): All subtasks must complete.
```
"Ship the USD pipeline"
|- [AND] Asset ingestion working
|- [AND] Layer composition correct
|- [AND] Render delegate connected
\- [AND] Performance within budget
-> ALL must succeed. Failure of any blocks the whole.
```

### Value = Hardest Remaining Subtask
From AlphaProof: back-propagate the value of the hardest branch, not the average. When working an AND-node task, identify and surface the hardest subtask early. Don't let easy wins mask a lurking blocker.

**ADHD integration:** This directly fights the tendency to do easy tasks first and avoid the hard one. Surface the blocker, name it, then apply MicroCommitment Engine to it.

### Too-Easy Heuristic
If a complex problem resolves suspiciously fast, verify the framing before celebrating:
- Problem was simpler than it seemed (good)
- We solved a different problem than intended (verify)
- Missing edge case or constraint (check)

### Test-Time Adaptation
When stuck on a hard problem, generate variations:
1. Simplified version -- removes a constraint
2. Partial solution -- solves a subset
3. Analogous problem -- same pattern, different domain

**ADHD integration:** This IS the MicroCommitment Engine with formal justification. You're not "avoiding the hard thing" -- you're building a curriculum that converges on it.

### Scalable Search Depth
```
Attempt 1: Quick pattern match (@napkin/@proto depth) -> Solved? Done. Survived? Escalate.
Attempt 2: Structured analysis (@alpha depth) -> Solved? Done. Survived? Escalate.
Attempt 3: Deep multi-pass (@rigorous/@prod depth) -> Solved? Done. Survived? Surface as genuinely hard.
```

Integration with depth gradients: @proto->small search | @alpha->medium search | @prod->large search | @research->maximal search

